/// RFC-0099 — a generator reports a diagnostic.
///
/// `table("./data/users.tbl")` runs at load time, emits an ordinary module, and
/// WARNS about line 3 of the table definition:
///
///     data/users.tbl:3:7: warning: column `email` has no length limit; write `String(120)`
///
/// The warning rides a build that succeeded: the program below runs, prints, and
/// exits 0 exactly as it would if the generator had nothing to say. `vyrn build
/// --deny-warnings` is how a project refuses it instead.
///
/// Nothing in the compiler knows what a table or a length limit is. The rule
/// lives in `lib/gen_table.vyrn`, in Vyrn, and any generator can write its own.
///
/// Inspect the synthesized module with:  vyrn emit-gen examples/gentable.vyrn
import { table } from "./lib/gen_table"
import { columnCount, columnNames } from table("./data/users.tbl")

fn main() -> Int64 {
    print(columnCount())
    print(columnNames())
    return 0
}
